adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) { ... }
```

There is no guard that `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is configured to a non-empty value. Since `.env.example` sets `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""` by default, a self-hoster could deploy with an empty secret; in that case an attacker can send the chosen header with an empty value and the comparison will succeed, effectively disabling authentication for this endpoint.

The timing-attack portion is also technically true: `!==` on strings is not constant-time, so it can leak information about the secret through timing (even if practical exploitability over the network is limited).
